In article <3ughik$bf0@wmwap1.math.uni-wuppertal.de>,
Andreas Hetfeld <HETFELD@WEEEV3.UNI-WUPPERTAL.DE> wrote:
>
>how can I configure a 'PC-keyboard' on an alpha-station like a DEC-keyboard
>for using the keypad as used in lse/edt etc.?
>

The only answer we could find was to order our Alpha-stations with DEC
VT-style keyboards, i.e. ones with a gold key at top-left of the
right-hand block of keys, rather than the stupid NUM-LOCK.  It took a lot
of effort to find out that this could even be done - you need to be
really persistent, and we got conflicting stories from various DEC
offices about it first.  The proof is that we now have the right
keyboards and they work.
