Subject: ALPHA's, OSF1, AdvFS, & INN.
Date: 1995/07/26
Message-ID: <3v5hr6$320@chaos.dac.neu.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 106869402
summary: AdvFS failures & news.
organization: Northeastern University, Boston, MA. 02115, USA
keywords: AdvFS news failure recovery
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.osf.misc

     We've been having a terrible time with AdvFS on our APLHA 4000
since it arrived over a year ago.  Digital Equipment has tried many
times to fix the problems, sometimes sending as many as 60 to 70
"patches" at a shot, without success.  I am now considering whether to
run INN on another APLHA with the AdvFS.  DEC has claimed that the
failures we see are related to the very large number of small files on
our current system.  This sounds very reminisent of news, i.e. generally
speaking a very large number of small files (not counting alt.binaries
of course:-).

     Oviously I don't want to lose all my news in one gulp, especially
if I'm keeping a week or more of the stuff.  But at this point I a) don't 
really trust AdvFS and b) don't trust DEC to get the bloody thing fixed
properly (I'm not even sure they have any clue as to what's wrong.
Yes the problem has been escalated.  No it hasn't helped.).

     I'd be very interested in talking to people who run INN on an ALPHA
with OSF/1 (or Digital UNIX or whatever they call it this week) using AdvFS.
I'm curious about AdvFS failure rates, news losage during failure,
recovery, how you have your news tree structured on AdvFS, if you're
even using AdvFS with INN, if not then why,etc.  

     And anything else you can think of that might help my decision
making process would be good.

     Any help greatly appreciated as always.  Thank you.

