In article <3unuq7$idm@fstgds15.tu-graz.ac.at>,
tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at (Thomas Leitner) writes:
tom> Why not just try to copy the /usr/sbin/nfsd file from an V3.0
tom> machine and use it under V3.2?

Much of the implementation of nfsd is in the kernel; the daemon is
largely there to provide a process context for the kernel to do
various things in.  Mixing nfsd between versions can be a recipe for
disaster, especially if the implementation changed significantly
