DEC FUSE comes with a debugger GUI which will work with either 
DECladebug or dbx as the underlying engine.  In the next release of
Digital Unix, the DECladebug subsets will include the GUI for free.
This version of the GUI will not work with dbx, as it will be linked
directly to the DECladebug engine using an API.  The benefit of this
is speed.

If you are an emacs diehard like myself, you might also try using
decladebug.el, from /usr/opt/LDB*/emacs/lisp/decladebug.el.  This will
give you a character-cell interface with source line scrolling.  It
has the advantage of when you find the bug, you are pointing at with
emacs and can make the change right there, to a M-x compile and you're
off.

Regards,
Tim
