Some approximate answers....

ptonkin@colesmyer.com.au (Peter Tonkin CMIS) wrote:
>Hi,
>	I would like to know if anyone can tell me about DCE security 
>	
>	Does it support ?
>
>
>	1. password lifetime,  length,  expiry from windows client

Basically yes.

>	2. Oracle Databases

 If you mean does Oracle hand its security over to DCE, then no.  DCE manages
access to DCE server interfaces.  In a three-tier architecture, this usually
means security on business functionality, not the data itself.

>	3. Shrink wrapped client/server applications 

Sound like you are looking for some sort of Single Sign On (SSO).  DCE does not
offer SSO by magic.  Shrink wrapped applications **could** choose to use DCE or
vanilla kerberos security, in which case DCE security **could** be used, but
DCE doesn't automagically take over the security for some application.


>
>Thanks,
>	Peter	
>		

