In article <DBnJIu.4Bx@colesmyer.com.au>,
Peter Tonkin CMIS <ptonkin@colesmyer.com.au> wrote:
>Hi,
>	I would like to know if anyone can tell me about DCE security 

First off, you would do better to post a question like this to:
   comp.soft-sys.dce  which is dedicated to DCE.

>	Does it support ?
>	1. password lifetime,  length,  expiry from windows client

Some capabilities are available today.  They are substantially improved
in DCE 1.1 available from vendors later this year.

>	2. Oracle Databases

The question is not does DCE support Oracle, but does Oracle support DCE?
The answer is: not too well.  Two new features in DCE 1.1 will make it easier
for vendors to support DCE, but they will still have to do it.  This is more
a perception and market share issue than a technical issue.  The ideal would
be for a product, such as a database, to accept a DCE PAC and map it onto
their existing access control model.

>	3. Shrink wrapped client/server applications 

There are some vendors selling products on DCE.  Peoplesoft is one and I
believe that there is a financial package as well.  It is also relatively
easy to integrate anything that uses OLE or VBX with DCE apps.  Also,
depending on your point of view, DFS is an off-the-shelf product that
offers consderable advantages over the alternatives.

