On Solaris 2, Unixware 2, Sinix, and DG-UX the standard installation
software is pkgadd, pkginfo, ...  This seems to be a system V thing.
Is there any talk about standardizing on the software installation
tool for Digital Unix?  I think that this sould be something that
X/Open, Spec 1170, POSIX ... sould address, does it?  One installation
tool that is the same across all platforms would go over big with
sysadmins.  This would allow much easier plug and play software.  Now
it seems that for each software package that is added, the sysadmin
must learn a new software installation tool.  One standard software
maintance/installation tool would be cool.

Any answers?

Thanks.



